# armour/man/plate: steel plate on the man (P2c slice, SLICE-ARMOUR; STYLE_P2 25.2-25.3, 26): a gorget, a breastplate in
# broad planes (the lit plane step 3, the turn step 2, the shadow step 1, the silhouette step 0) with ONE lit ridge (a step-4
# run on the keel facing down and up, on the lit edge facing right and left: the glint jumps to the new lit side as the body
# turns), its lower edge shadowing a fauld lame at the waist. The tassets ride the hang channel (plate_hang), the pauldrons
# the shoulders (shared/pauldron_plate_*); arms and legs take metal by region (the resolver's region slots).
# Keys: every key the torso channel takes (rest idle run runl drawn swing lie) in D U R L; side runl is the run with the
# method's lean rows (from 4 under the neck a pixel back, from 7 two); the L lie is the lying chest. Left views painted.
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body man
role armour plate
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2

